  "purpose": "A-priori (unfitted) head-to-head of two published cohesive-energy chi models on the module's in-tree external-validation corpus (8 published polymer-solvent chi values, Van Krevelen 1990 Table 7.6 / Bawn 1949 / Sakurada 1954 / Krigbaum 1959 / Malcolm-Rowlinson 1957): the incumbent Hansen three-component parameter (dD/dP/dH) versus the single Hildebrand solubility parameter delta_total. The two models share an identical entropic term (0.34) and identical prefactor V_s/(RT); ONLY the cohesive-distance metric differs, so the comparison isolates the value of resolving cohesion into three components. The prefactor is back-derived from the already-signed Hansen receipt, reproducing its chi column byte-exactly (known-answer bind) before the Hildebrand column is swapped in.",
